  description: "It is 11pm. Your SDET final-round interview is tomorrow for a high-traffic platform that serves millions of API requests per day. You have rehearsed your Playwright framework design, your CI/CD pipeline strategy, your contract testing approach. Then your eye catches the job description again: 'Experience testing rate-limited and throttled API endpoints in automated test suites.' Your stomach tightens. You have never written a test that deals with a 429 Too Many Requests response. You do not know what a token bucket algorithm looks like from a testing perspective. You cannot explain how to mock rate limits or test exponential backoff logic. You have never validated Retry-After headers or X-RateLimit-Remaining counts. Mitchell Agoma's 20-year enterprise testing guide — forged in the high-traffic systems at HMRC, MoD, Nationwide, Asda, Co-op, BT, and Accenture where API rate limits are not theoretical edge cases but production incidents waiting to happen — covers every rate limiting and throttling testing interview question you will face, from token bucket vs sliding window architectures to testing retry strategies, from mocking 429 responses in CI to validating rate limit headers, from concurrent request testing to circuit breaker integration. This is the guide for the SDET who just realised their test suite has never encountered a rate limit — and their interviewer definitely will.",
