  description: "It is 11pm. Your final-round SDET interview is in nine hours for a fintech platform that processes sensitive customer data behind Google Authenticator MFA. You have prepped Playwright, API testing, CI/CD pipelines, and test strategy. But then you remember the single sentence in the technical requirements: 'Experience testing multi-factor authentication flows in automated test suites.' Your stomach drops. You have never automated a 2FA login. You do not know the difference between TOTP and HOTP. You cannot explain how to bypass MFA in a CI pipeline without compromising security. You have never tested a biometric authenticator flow. Mitchell Agoma's 20-year enterprise testing guide — built from real MFA testing projects at HMRC, MoD, Nationwide, Asda, Co-op, and BT — covers every authentication testing interview question you will face, from TOTP seed management to SMS OTP mocking, from biometric WebAuthn testing to magic link flows, from CI/CD MFA bypass strategies to session token reuse patterns. This is the guide for the SDET whose automation framework gets blocked at the login screen.",
