      a: "Multi-currency testing covers: (1) Presentment currency — the currency the customer sees and pays in (e.g. EUR). (2) Settlement currency — the currency the business receives (e.g. GBP). Stripe can handle the conversion automatically. My tests verify: the PaymentIntent is created with the correct presentment currency and amount, Stripe's response includes the conversion rate and settlement amount, my system records both the presentment and settlement amounts correctly, and the customer's receipt shows the correct presentment currency while my accounting system records the settlement currency. I also test edge cases: zero-decimal currencies (JPY, where amounts are integers without decimal places), three-decimal currencies (BHD, where Stripe requires amounts in the smallest unit but some gateways handle sub-cent precision differently), and the scenario where a customer's card issuer charges a foreign transaction fee — this is outside my system's control, but I verify my UI communicates clearly about which currency the customer will be charged in.",
