      q: "What's the difference between canary deployment testing and blue-green deployment testing?",
      a: "Canary deployment testing distributes testing across the rollout — health checks, smoke tests, and canary analysis (metrics comparison) run progressively as traffic increases from 5% to 100%. Blue-green deployment testing front-loads all testing before the traffic switch — full regression, integration, and performance testing in the green environment — then switches all traffic at once. Canary testing catches production-specific issues (real traffic patterns, production-scale data, cross-service interactions) that staging environments miss; blue-green testing requires more comprehensive pre-switch testing because the blast radius of a bad deployment is 100% of users immediately. Choose canary when you practice continuous delivery with frequent, backward-compatible deployments; choose blue-green when you need instant rollback, can't run two versions simultaneously, or have compliance requirements that mandate full pre-release validation."
