      "q": "What is the difference between AI coding assistants and AI test automation tools?",
      "a": "AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor, CodeWhisperer) are general-purpose developer tools that assist with writing, reviewing, and refactoring code — including test code. They operate at the code level: generating test functions, suggesting assertions, scaffolding frameworks. AI test automation tools (self-healing locators, AI-powered visual diffing, autonomous test agents with MCP) are testing-specific tools that automate testing tasks: healing broken selectors, comparing screenshots with AI, and executing tests autonomously. The interview-ready distinction: AI coding assistants help you write better tests faster; AI test automation tools help you run and maintain tests with less human intervention. A mature AI testing strategy uses both — AI coding assistants for test development, AI test automation tools for test execution and maintenance — and understands the risk profile of each category. For more on AI test automation tools, see our guide on <a href=\"/blog/ai-in-testing-interview-questions-2026\">AI in testing interview questions</a>."
